<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES FROM FAIRYHOUSE.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES FROM FAIRYHOUSE.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of grade one feature races</p>
<p>run at Fairyhouse on Sunday:</p>
<p>Royal Bond Novice Hurdle run over two miles (3.2 kms)</p>
<p>1. Istabraq 11-8 favourite (ridden by Charlie Swan)</p>
<p>2. Palette 14-1 (David Casey)</p>
<p>3. Noble Thyne 13-8 (Tommy Treacy0</p>
<p>Seven ran.</p>
<p>Distances: 4-1/2 lengths, 15 lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by John McManus and trained in Ireland by Aidan</p>
<p>O'Brien.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner:  16,250 Irish punts ($25,220</p>
<p>dollars)</p>
<p>Drinmore Novice Steeplechase run over two and a half miles</p>
<p>(4 kms)</p>
<p> 1. Doran's Pride	 5-4 favourite (Richard Dunwoody)</p>
<p> 2. See More Business   5-2 (Tony McCoy)</p>
<p>3. Executive Options  14-1 (Carl Llewellyn)</p>
<p>Eight ran.</p>
<p>Distances: one length, distance.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Tom Doran and trained in Ireland by Michael</p>
<p>Hourigan.</p>
<p>Value to winner: $35,000.</p>
<p>Hatton's Grace Hurdle, run over two and a half miles (4-km)</p>
<p>1. Large Action 9-4 (Jamie Osborne)</p>
<p>2. Cockney Lad 8-1 (Richard Hughes)</p>
<p>3. Theatreworld 6-4 favourite (Charlie Swan)</p>
<p>Eight ran</p>
<p>Distances: six lengths, one length, 25 lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Brian Stewart-Brown and trained by Oliver</p>
<p>Sherwood in England. Value to winner 26,000 Irish pounds</p>
<p>($43,700)</p>
</text>
